b.com/sindresorhus/stringify-attributes/issues"},"author":{"name":"Sindre Sorhus","email":"sindresorhus@gmail.com","url":"https://sindresorhus.com"},"license":"MIT","homepage":"https://github.com/sindresorhus/stringify-attributes#readme","keywords":["html","attributes","stringify","element","tag","props","object","convert","transform"],"repository":{"type":"git","url":"git+https://github.com/sindresorhus/stringify-attributes.git"},"description":"Turn an object into a string of HTML attributes","maintainers":[{"name":"sindresorhus","email":"sindresorhus@gmail.com"}],"readme":"# stringify-attributes\n\n> Turn an object into a string of HTML attributes\n\n## Install\n\n```sh\nnpm install stringify-attributes\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n```js\nimport stringifyAttributes from 'stringify-attributes';\n\nstringifyAttributes({\n\tunicorn: '🦄',\n\trainbow: true,\n\tnumber: 1,\n\tmultiple: [\n\t\t'a',\n\t\t'b'\n\t]\n});\n//=> ' unicorn=\"🦄\" rainbow number=\"1\" multiple=\"a b\"'\n```\n\nNote that the string is prepended with a space when there are attributes to simplify using it in a HTML tag.\n\n## Related\n\n- [create-html-element](https://github.com/sindresorhus/create-html-element) - Create a HTML element string\n","readmeFilename":"readme.md","users":{"rocket0191":true,"flumpus-dev":true}}